---
description: "When to use installed MCPs and Cursor tools instead of guessing or doing it manually"
alwaysApply: false
---

- For anything involving live database schema, data, or migrations: use the Supabase/Neon MCP to check actual state rather than assuming from memory of the code.
- For GitHub actions (issues, PRs, branches): use the GitHub MCP/tools rather than instructing me to run manual git commands, where available.
- Before answering questions about "does X exist in this project" or "what does this table look like," check via the relevant MCP/tool instead of guessing from partial context.
- If a task would clearly benefit from an installed MCP but it isn't being used, say so explicitly rather than working around it manually.
